WEBVTT

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:03.100
Me?

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:07.500
I'm gonna be their manager?!

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.760
In training.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.450
You'll be supporting LIP×LIP with me.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:13.900
No one told us that!

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.560
I told you we'd be hiring temps because

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.700
there's so much to do before 
your summer concert, remember?

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.010
But why is <i>she</i> the temp?

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.250
You said you "don't care about idols."

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.830
U-Um...

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:30.620
You realize she didn't 
even know we were idols?!

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:33.410
She's obviously unfit to be our manager!

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:36.180
Agreed. She'll never hack it.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.680
You don't know that. I haven't even—

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.180
It's obvious.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:44.730
Why did you start to tell the whole 
class you saw me at the police station?

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.270
I wasn't thinking...

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:52.320
You just blurted out what you saw.
 That's beyond insensitive.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.320
She's a nosy little dimwit.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.550
She's awkward and can't read social cues.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.860
And she's naïve to boot.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:04.200
You're only in sync at times like these.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.920
I'm simply stating the facts.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.710
She lacks delicacy and tact.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.630
She's got no taste, and she's a potato face!

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.260
Can it, you two!

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:15.820
You talk like you're so much better than me,

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:17.930
insultin' me to my face after ya just met me!

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:20.260
Clearly <i>you're</i> the insensitive one!

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:24.100
You paste on a phony smile for 
girls ya don't even want around,

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.070
so <i>you're</i> the tasteless one!

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.270
You call yourselves "idols"?

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:32.270
Even if every other high school 
girl in Japan loves you...

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:34.240
I don't!

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:46.300
<i>I'm an idiot! Did I just get myself 
fired from a 1,500-per-hour job?!</i>

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:49.420
We were right about you. You've got guts.

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.480
LIP×LIP may be all the rage 
with high school girls,

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:59.040
but Hiyoko here doesn't see the appeal.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:03.990
Er, my name isn't Hiyoko. It's Hiyori.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:07.390
Clearly there's plenty of room 
for the LIP×LIP fandom to grow.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:08.820
I like a challenge.

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:12.110
All right, fine.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.770
Let her be manager-in-training, 
if that's what she wants.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:17.810
Hey!

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:19.700
It's only until summer.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.370
However!

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:27.540
We don't need dead weight, 
so prove your worth.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.000
I will! I'll get the job done!

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:33.500
Just wait! I'll make you admit my worth!

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.540
<b>Heroines Run the Show</b>

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.930
<b>Guidance Office</b>

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:09.590
I'm turning in a job 
permission form. Please sign it.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:13.580
Um, as for what I'll be doing...

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.290
I'm okaying it.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.810
Akechi Saku

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:16.810
<b>Akechi</b>

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:19.880
Huh? You are?

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:24.050
CEO Tamura called me yesterday 
and explained the situation.

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:26.820
Oh, good.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.680
Please don't tell anyone I'm their manager.

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:34.290
I know the deal.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:41.610
Teaching idols must be tough too, huh?

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:47.280
They're students like the rest of you. 
I'll help them enjoy school life.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.400
That's really all.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:53.180
<i>Akechi-sensei is a wonderful teacher!</i>

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:57.900
You should come to me whenever 
you have troubles too, Suzumi.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:00.110
Now do your best.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:03.360
Yes, sir!

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:18.130
<i>Studying, the team, chores...</i>

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:19.590
<i>I'm busy 24/7.</i>

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:22.760
<i>But I expected that, so it's fine.</i>

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.590
<i>What I didn't expect is...</i>

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.910
That's a wrap, thanks!

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:42.940
Hey!

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:45.310
Hurry up and put that away.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:46.990
We're on to the next studio.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:51.140
These are heavy! 
I'm s'posed to carry them all?

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:52.670
Duh.

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:55.290
Carrying stuff is Management 101.

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.000
<b>\hAizo-sama
Yujiro-sama</b>

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.440
Hot coffee.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.900
Cocoa with milk.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:00.750
Huh?

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.270
Go <i>buy</i> them!

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:03.400
ASAP.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:09.720
<i>This manager-in-training job 
pays well, but it pisses me off.</i>

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:14.550
Here I am again, Aizo.

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:15.930
You're always welcome.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:18.150
Can I have your autograph, Yujiro?

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:19.020
Of course.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:24.520
<i>They're surrounded during 
break times every day.</i>

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:28.450
I'm gonna visit Juri-chan.

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:36.540
Suzumi-san, are you okay?

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.120
Uh, sure...

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.330
You're so nice, Yujiro!

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:42.530
Don't just ditch us.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.800
U-Um...

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:50.320
Oh, I just remembered!

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:56.060
Someya-kun, Shibasaki-kun, 
Akechi-sensei was lookin' for you... I think!

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:59.010
You should've done that sooner.

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:02.120
Exactly. How clueless can you be?

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:04.400
You say that now, but...

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.510
I figured I shouldn't interrupt you.

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:10.280
It's like that every break! 
Anyone would be annoyed!

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:13.000
Training or not, you're a manager,
 so use your head.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:16.080
Right, sorry.

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:20.910
Why do girls keep swarming us?
 It's seriously a pain.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:26.750
Because they're your fans. 
Isn't having lots of fans a good thing?

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:30.340
I'm uncomfortable with them.

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:31.360
Huh?

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:33.980
You're still saying that?

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:36.940
Being uncomfortable around 
girls is fatal for an idol.

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:40.170
Shut up! And <i>your</i> surliness 
is showing through!

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:41.480
Your face is a Noh mask!

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:45.060
This is just my face! 
And <i>you're</i> too glib with them!

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:45.930
Excuse me?

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:46.960
Excuse you!

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:50.530
Hold up!

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:52.480
No fighting!

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.060
Whatever, I'm out.

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:08.420
<i>Uncomfortable around girls...</i>

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:10.310
<i>Surly...</i>

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:14.340
<i>Why are they pop idols?</i>

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:21.270
The starting dash is key!

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.730
Hey, no running in the halls.

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:26.540
Yes, sir!

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:33.530
I'm late again.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:37.450
Hiya, Hiyori!

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:38.850
Juri-chan!

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:42.540
You bought a sandwich again.
 How do you do it?

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:44.580
There's a trick to it.

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:45.210
Oh?

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:49.380
The line at the end is your chance. 
It's shorter than the others.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:51.790
Always attack the least defended area.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:53.330
Okay!

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:08.490
<i>Yay, I got here! Thank you, Juri-chan!</i>

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.360
<b>Menu</b>

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.360
<b>Mixed Sandwich</b>

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.360
<b>Cutlet Sandwich</b>

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.360
<b>Ham Sandwich</b>

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.360
<b>Curry Bread</b>

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.360
Cutlet sandwich...

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:15.160
No, no, I gotta be frugal this month.

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:19.320
Let's see, what's cheapest?

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:19.320
<b>Anpan
Egg Salad Bun 
Deal!</b>

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.700
Egg salad, please!

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:27.490
It's so good.

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:30.550
Bun sandwiches are the best!

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:35.130
Suzumi-san, you seem busy lately. 
You're always running around.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:38.000
Do you do something after school?

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.220
Huh?

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:42.680
You being a manager-in-training 
has to be top secret.

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:45.640
You can't tell your friends or family.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:51.390
W-Well, I'm on the track team, 
you know? I just always run!

00:09:57.130 --> 00:10:00.610
<i>I've always been bad at keeping secrets...</i>

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.380
Oh, wow!

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:14.800
Running is so much fun!

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:17.820
Suzumi-san, I think you 
tied your personal best.

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:19.720
Oh, you're right!

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:22.300
Burning off stress gave me power!

00:10:28.490 --> 00:10:30.770
Sorry, Hina. Are you okay?

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:34.310
Sheesh, you almost hit my first-year!

00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:36.180
But I didn't, so it's fine!

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:40.780
You still startled her. 
You need to make it up to her.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:45.320
Okay, well... wanna get 
something to eat? My treat.

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:46.760
Yay!

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:50.370
Suzumi-san, want to go 
eat crêpes? It's Kotaro's treat!

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:52.320
Crêpes?!

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:57.400
Yes! I've always wanted to eat 
crêpes after school, and—ugh!

00:10:58.390 --> 00:11:01.240
I have work today...

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:03.470
Aw, that's a shame.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:09.390
Please ask me again sometime. 
Please! Promise me!

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:10.900
S-Sure.

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:20.450
My crêpe!

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:27.070
It's "Evenings with Full Throttle4!"

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:31.000
Good evening, everyone. 
This is Full Throttle4's RIO and...

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:33.690
...YUI speaking! Yay!

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:36.370
"Full Throttle4"?

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:38.640
You seriously haven't heard of them?

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:41.490
Huh? No...

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:47.130
Full Throttle4, or FT4 for short.

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:51.520
They're a talented song and dance unit. 
They're incredibly popular.

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:55.480
Study up on the industry if 
you want to be a manager.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:58.940
I'm sorry...

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:02.830
We have guests in the studio today.

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:04.800
It's LIP×LIP!

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:08.320
Good evening. This is LIP×LIP's Aizo...

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:12.330
...and Yujiro. It's good to see 
you again, RIO-san and YUI-san.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.600
Here's a brief reintroduction to LIP×LIP.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:19.460
The commercial they starred 
in was a hot topic,

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:22.010
and their debut single 
"Romeo" was their big break.

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:25.530
I saw your last concert! 
That was some big energy.

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:28.280
Our whole band went, and we had a good time.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.020
Thank you!

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:33.350
Those words from you two are quite an honor.

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:37.320
So, you got your debut through an 
audition sponsored by your agency.

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:39.340
Yes, we applied.

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:43.550
We were on the jury for that event. 
You both left a big impression.

00:12:43.550 --> 00:12:46.530
I voted for you too, 
so you'd better be grateful.

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:50.990
Thank you. We couldn't 
have debuted without you.

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:53.960
What made you want to be pop idols?

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:58.670
I wanted to be able to entertain 
people with my singing and dancing.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:02.860
Making our fans happy is 
what keeps us motivated.

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:05.880
You're lying.

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:13.310
You're lying.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:21.480
Sorry, but please stop 
recording for a moment.

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:24.560
Ow! What was that for, RIO?!

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:28.260
I told you not to say anything 
that would ruin LIP×LIP's image!

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:32.160
But they're saying all this 
boring "honor student" stuff!

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:35.000
They're just playing the part!
It's so not entertaining!

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:36.860
Ow, ow! I give, I give!

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:38.010
I'll stop.

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:39.200
Show remorse.

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:42.340
Sheesh, I was just saying what I thought.

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:45.380
Ow, ow, ow!

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:46.050
We'll have that part cut.

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:48.890
I apologize for YUI's rudeness.

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:50.770
It's all right.

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:52.600
We aren't taking it personally.

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:56.060
You aren't?

00:13:58.340 --> 00:14:01.360
On the stage, it doesn't matter 
whether you're new kids or veterans.

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:05.290
If your performance isn't exciting,
 your audience leaves.

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:10.240
If smiles are all you've got, 
you won't last long in this business.

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:13.330
You guys aren't gonna beat us.

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:17.200
We'll work hard so that we can 
share a stage with you soon.

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:20.670
Thank you for your valuable advice.

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:23.730
Later!

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:24.960
Thanks for coming.

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:26.750
Thank you very much.

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:28.220
Have a good night!

00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:35.110
Gee, sorry to be <i>boring</i>.

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:37.820
It's not like "playing the part"
 was our idea!

00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:39.980
We'll put those jerks out of business.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:43.440
<i>Out of business? Idols are scary!</i>

00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:57.900
I wonder what the lunch deal is today!

00:14:57.900 --> 00:14:59.830
What did you just say to me?!

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:07.180
<i>They're arguin' again!</i>

00:15:07.180 --> 00:15:10.630
<i>I wanna stay away. But...</i>

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:14.620
Keeping an eye on them at school is 
part of the manager-in-training's job.

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:18.940
Factoring that time into 
your pay... here's the total.

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:20.600
Whoa!

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:22.310
I'm doing this to live!

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:26.360
Hey! No fight—

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:32.860
Ow...

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:34.340
That hurt.

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:35.740
Are you picking a fight?

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:37.490
I-I'm sorry.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:39.100
But no fightin'!

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:40.120
Shut up.

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:41.080
Mind your own business.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.810
So you don't mind trashin' LIP×LIP's image?

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:47.380
Plus, you'll get suspended if they 
catch you fightin' at school!

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:50.400
So what? I don't wanna be here anyway.

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:51.340
Huh?

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:54.800
The CEO hired us on the condition

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:58.580
that we attend and graduate 
from a normal school.

00:15:59.150 --> 00:16:01.420
I wouldn't come to a place 
like this otherwise.

00:16:06.470 --> 00:16:08.730
"A place like this"?

00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:13.410
<i>I was really lookin' forward to high school.</i>

00:16:14.050 --> 00:16:20.500
<i>I wanted to make friends, be on the 
team, eat a crêpe on my way home...</i>

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:22.960
<i>There are so many fun things to do.</i>

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:24.450
<i>But...</i>

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:27.760
<i>I guess they don't feel that way.</i>

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:26.880
<b>Nonfantasy</b>

00:16:34.420 --> 00:16:36.220
I don't get it.

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:43.140
Sort and organize these 
fan letters and presents.

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:45.330
It's part of a manager's job.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:47.420
All of these?

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:48.940
Yes. Thanks!

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:55.840
Who knew so many people 
were cheerin' for them?

00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:58.710
Aizo...

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:03.120
Yujiro...

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:06.650
This is for both of them.

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:08.860
Is this hand-made?!

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:13.160
And it... smells really good...

00:17:13.160 --> 00:17:14.130
Wow!

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:17.510
<b>Chutan</b>

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:17.510
Chutan-san...

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:18.620
Wait...

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:22.830
This is Chutan-san, too.

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:28.400
<b>To LIP×LIP's Manager</b>

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:28.400
"To LIP×LIP's Manager"?

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:33.830
Hello, Uchida-san!

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:37.350
Hi, Hiyoko. All done?

00:17:37.350 --> 00:17:39.360
Yep, more or less.

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:42.460
Um, here...

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:46.620
Oh, it's Chutan-san.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:50.340
Chutan-san has been a passionate 
LIP×LIP fan since their debut.

00:17:51.060 --> 00:17:53.630
They even write letters to me and the CEO,

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:56.080
asking us to take good care of LIP×LIP.

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:59.760
Huh. So, where are those two?

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:01.670
In a lesson.

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:29.910
Fightin' again...

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:33.290
Pick a drink, Hiyoko.

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:36.340
Oh! Orange juice, please.

00:18:39.690 --> 00:18:41.770
So, are you getting used to the job?

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:46.200
I s'pose. They insult me constantly, though.

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:49.210
It's not funny!

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:51.400
That's not a bad thing.

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:55.690
Aizo is uncomfortable around girls, 
and Yujiro rarely drops his game face,

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:58.670
yet they show <i>you</i> their true selves.

00:18:58.670 --> 00:18:59.650
True selves?

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:03.670
The first task of a manager 
is to know her artists.

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:08.530
But if all that's happenin' is that 
they don't treat me as a girl...

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:11.330
You have a point.

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:16.300
I don't really get it.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:20.720
Why are those two idols?

00:19:22.330 --> 00:19:26.430
I asked them about their motivations 
during the audition. They said...

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:28.060
I want to sing.

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:30.270
I want to be on stage.

00:19:31.180 --> 00:19:32.290
Why?

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:36.020
I don't know the details. They won't tell me.

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:39.740
But they never whine, 
and they never compromise.

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:44.010
I'm sure their desire to 
be pop idols is genuine.

00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:48.660
The "idol smile" isn't easy, you know.

00:19:52.270 --> 00:19:55.630
<i>I don't know much about idols.</i>

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:59.380
<i>And I don't know what those two are thinkin'.</i>

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:04.510
<i>But I can kinda tell one thing.</i>

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:09.430
<i>There's something they wanna do, 
and they don't wanna give it up.</i>

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:14.850
<i>That "I won't back down no matter 
what anyone says" feeling...</i>

00:20:16.010 --> 00:20:21.370
<i>Maybe bein' idols means to 
them what runnin' means to me.</i>

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:25.210
Look at the time!

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:27.600
Hiyoko, you can call it a night.

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:28.530
Yes, ma'am.

00:20:29.010 --> 00:20:30.970
Have a good night!

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:43.680
That's all for today!

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:47.760
Good work today!

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:49.810
What are you doing here?

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:52.770
You should go home as soon 
as you're done working.

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:56.190
Honestly, why are you so mean?

00:20:56.520 --> 00:21:00.130
Anyone would tell you the same. 
Do you know what time it is?

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:03.030
You're technically a girl, Potato Face.

00:21:04.600 --> 00:21:08.160
<i>That's surprisingly considerate.</i>

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:10.490
Um...

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:12.070
Here!

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:15.930
I got you coffee and cocoa with milk.

00:21:15.930 --> 00:21:20.640
Seriously? People want water or 
sports drinks after a lesson!

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:22.630
Nobody wants hot coffee.

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:25.340
You figured just bringing drinks 
we like was good enough,

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:28.010
without even considering our circumstances.

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:30.540
The sheer simple-mindedness irritates me.

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:35.980
Wait, don't you want these?

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:39.610
No!

00:21:43.470 --> 00:21:45.990
<i>Idols...</i>

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:50.950
<i>seriously piss me off!</i>

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:54.950
<b>Episode 2</b>

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:54.950
<b>The Manager-in-Training Job!</b>

00:23:26.320 --> 00:23:32.890
Next time, on episode 3 of 
<i>Heroines Run the Show</i>...

00:23:32.890 --> 00:23:34.310
"Nonfantasy"!

00:23:33.860 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Episode 3
 Nonfantasy</b>
